  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amol Ambadas Bhosale vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 861.25aba etc (1) In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 861 Of 2025 Santosh @ Bandu Pandharinath Nawale Versus The State Of Maharashtra With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 862 Of 2025 Amol Ambadas Bhosale Versus The State Of Maharashtra ..... Mr A. R. Kawade, Advocate for Applicants. Mr M. K. Goyanka, App for respondent/State. ..... Coram : Advait M. Sethna, J. Date : 22 July 2025",
    "facts": "The FIR is lodged on 15/04/2025 at 15:20 hours with the Paithan Police Station, Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar (Gramin). The offences are registered under Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a), 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and 223, 274, 275, 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. Accused Nos.4 and 5 who have been 861.25aba etc (2) subsequently added as accused are before this Court. As per the FIR, Amol Ambadas Bhosale vs The State Of Maharashtra on 22 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/151325807/ 1 these applicants are named as accused. Further their names have also been taken by the co-accused persons. It appears that there are several orders passed in relation to this issue by the different Courts. It is submitted that seizure panchnama is filed and the learned APP would not dispute that the alleged contraband is recovered.",
    "arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Supreme Court has recently passed an order in Special Leave to Appeal (Cri.) No.8698/2023 in the case of Eknath Bhalchandra Patil Vs. The State of Maharashtra, where the Supreme Court in its order dated 28/07/2023 has categorically observed that the Petitioner therein shall not be arrested in connection with Crime No.354/2022, subject to condition that he shall cooperate with the investigation. The Supreme Court has also observed that the issue regarding applicability of Section 123 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita [Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code] is pending before the Supreme Court."
  },
